# Native YouTube Music provider

GPL-3.0. Catalog parsing and the original guest integration were adapted from MetroList at commit e97197786c2a7ad56279cc9bb4ce3233ef6c99ff. The standalone account, Home, JSON client configuration and plugin transport work are maintained by 956tris. YouTube Music Video Canvas lookup (`YouTubeCanvas.kt`, resolving `/next` video counterparts and YouTube Music video search/streams) is adapted from MetroList (`https://github.com/MetrolistGroup/Metrolist`, GPL-3.0): `MusicVideoCounterpart.kt`, `MusicVideoMatcher.kt`, and `AnimatedCoverSelection.kt`, with thanks to its contributors.

The build bundles InnerTubeX v0.11.7 from https://github.com/MetrolistGroup/innertubex/tree/v0.11.7 and QuackJS v0.1.4 from https://github.com/MetrolistGroup/quackjs/tree/v0.1.4. The host supplies Kotlin, coroutines, serialization, Ktor, Compose, MetroFuse API 1.1.0 and the plugin SDK. Production code uses platform HTTP engine discovery, including on Android. The plugin owns its network client and session and does not read the application's old YouTube account.

This implementation provides search, catalog, metadata, Home, WebView account sign-in and audio extraction. NativeLoginUi supplies the plugin-owned account screen through the reusable plugin SDK. The plugin owns its browser request and labels; SDK platform WebViews capture a candidate session and pass it only to the current activation's login callback. Authentication verifies an active account before committing credentials. The host stores credentials through its owner-scoped encrypted store. Failed account replacement preserves the previous session, and logout clears it. Login text is packaged in assets/login.json.

SABR sessions cross the public plugin API as the metrofuse.sabr.v1 JSON attribute on a SABR_UMP StreamDescriptor. The app validates the media identity, URL, format IDs and bounded session data, then creates its own InnerTubeX SabrBootstrap. Plugin-private classes are never passed into the app player.

Content locale comes from the system and host requests. Home titles come from the service. Library-linked Home shelves are excluded. Home feed pages, radio recommendations and account-library categories support continuations. Library includes songs, albums, artists and playlists. Liked Music pages and song votes use the plugin account; menu like status is preserved in track metadata. Only the initial search/catalog browse page is exposed. Channel switching, saving or removing library collections and music video playback remain outside this implementation. The radio, Home and Library test fixtures use synthetic identities and service renderer shapes and contain no account data.

See the repository README for builds, installation, verification and manual checks. JAR and APK files are published in GitHub Releases. The separate universal implementation in ../universal supports account, Home and direct audio without native payloads or full InnerTubeX player transforms.
